{
  "_comment": [
    "The catalogue you buy a kitchen from. Every station type has a cheap, a standard and a",
    "premium model.",
    "",
    "The premium tier is deliberately faster AND smaller per unit. That is what makes",
    "upgrading a real alternative to expanding: when the building is full, better equipment",
    "is the only way left to add throughput. A pile of cheap ovens is the beginner move and",
    "it eats the floor space your dining room needs.",
    "",
    "footprint is square metres per unit, including the clearance to actually work around it.",
    "platesAtOnce is how many plates ONE unit works at the same time -- a deck oven holds",
    "several pizzas, a four-burner range has four burners. Before this every cooking station",
    "was one plate at a time, so a deck oven made five pizzas an hour and the only way to",
    "grow throughput was to buy more boxes."
  ],
